1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,669
Same apple, same cut.

2
00:00:01,669 --> 00:00:04,273
So why is only one half going brown?

3
00:00:04,773 --> 00:00:05,641
It isn't rot.

4
00:00:05,641 --> 00:00:07,776
The apple is doing it to itself.

5
00:00:08,276 --> 00:00:09,755
Cutting bursts its cells.

6
00:00:10,055 --> 00:00:13,449
An enzyme spills out onto the fruit's own polyphenols.

7
00:00:13,949 --> 00:00:18,670
Add oxygen, and it turns them into quinones that clump into brown pigment.

8
00:00:19,170 --> 00:00:21,023
The white half got lemon juice.

9
00:00:21,323 --> 00:00:25,705
Acid slows the enzyme, and vitamin C undoes its first step.

10
00:00:26,205 --> 00:00:28,107
Would you still eat the brown half?
